hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"997","Bundar told us, Yahya bin Sa’id told us, Ibn Abi Adiy, Muhammad bin Ja’far, Sahl bin Yusuf, and Abd al-Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed, they said: Awf told us, on the authority of Abu Raja, he said: Imran bin Husayn told us, he said: We were on a journey with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He mentioned the hadith about them praying in their sleep until the sun rose, and he said: “Then he called for prayer and he led the people.”"
"998","Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn al-Nu’man narrated to us, Abu Ja’far al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Bilal, he said: “We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he slept until the sun rose, so he ordered Bilal, So he gave the call to prayer, so they performed ablution, then they prayed the two rak’ahs, then they prayed the morning prayer.” Abu Bakr said: In the news of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of his father, he said: So he ordered Bilal, and he gave the call to prayer, then he stood and led us in prayer."
